{"created_commit":"38fe488c4212f833349214f39ab336a55a80269c","created_generation":"001","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-001-pregeometric-pairwise.md"],"finding_id":"F001-PAIRWISE-RISE","literal_value":{"alphabet":"W4","support_not_weight":true},"magnitude_class":"moderate","notes":"functional_significance is unknown. The report localises the tension to this coordinate.","observable":"rise-then-release probability, stationary triangle mass, reversibility defect","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":3,"exactness":4,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":2,"replication":4},"scope":"Generation 1 pairwise grammar, W4, N=2 to N=5 within the declared K bounds","statement":"In the searched memoryless pairwise cells, reweighting moves stationary triangle mass and can break reversibility, and it does not move the predeclared 4-step rise-then-release probability for the same three-literal closing rule. That event tracks support rather than the soft weights.","status":"active","structural_roles":["expressiveness","negative_finding"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"f076f80612d8605eda9e7c04207e4c66d8e45dd6","created_generation":"003C","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-003c-memory-clock-refinement.md"],"finding_id":"F003-CLOCK-SPLIT","literal_value":{"epoch_defect":0,"full_event_positive_sets":"5250 of 7385"},"magnitude_class":"moderate","notes":"","observable":"full-event-clock memory TV and pair-event epoch memory TV","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":4,"replication":4},"scope":"Generation 3C memory-clock refinement, N=3 independent triad","statement":"Separating the full-event clock from the pair-event epoch shows that some apparent pairwise memory is hidden timing and some is a hidden transition law. On the pair-event clock the next pair event can still depend on the triad that rode along. The full process remains first-order Markov.","status":"active","structural_roles":["memory","gate"],"temporal_character":"local"}
{"created_commit":"0c9bf3a3f673b5f191e47ef46c6ac3ca10c0e414","created_generation":"004A","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-004a-reconfiguration-sensitivity.md"],"finding_id":"F004-PASSAGE-AFTER-OCCUPANCY","literal_value":{"median_occupancy_share_T_to_P":0.749762376955627,"range":[0.5861778688217765,1.0402273551834786]},"magnitude_class":"large","notes":"Float64 solver results are not called exact identities.","observable":"controlled eventual committor versus stationary eventual delta","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":4,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":4},"scope":"Generation 4a, 160 kernels, eventual committor on the pair-event epoch kernel","statement":"After source occupancy is separated from future dynamics, N=4 higher-order state still changes lower-order passage. On a typical T->P row most of the stationary eventual delta is occupancy. The controlled eventual remainder stays above the floor on all 40 T->P rows. The median occupancy share of that stationary delta is about 0.750.","status":"active","structural_roles":["occupancy_shift","routing"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"d8c97964850194577ecf084a0fb00c209378957c","created_generation":"005","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-005-targeted-tp-pp-pairs.md"],"finding_id":"F005-COMPOSITION-NOT-SUM","literal_value":{"example_interaction":-0.038757894038537355,"example_pair":"a242054905a5b0245e08de79"},"magnitude_class":"small","notes":"This is not the Generation 8 occupancy residual. The two are different observables.","observable":"interaction residual of the controlled eventual committor","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":4,"parameter_robustness":2,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":3},"scope":"Generation 5 targeted T->P and P->P pairs, N=4, O=3, H=0","statement":"One higher-order-conditioned pairwise rule and one ordinary pairwise rule do not add on the eventual passage between the two-edge path and the two-edge matching. On the strongest motif each rule alone barely moves the controlled committor, and the pair moves it by several hundredths in a source-dependent direction.","status":"active","structural_roles":["interaction"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"107c7ab30fb0a36ed992e78b637ba3fda7ec5d16","created_generation":"007","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-007-effect-matched-controls.md"],"finding_id":"F006-SCALAR-AGGREGATE","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"moderate","notes":"Qualified by the Generation 7B two-level census, which states the same split more sharply.","observable":"aggregate passage versus state-resolved passage","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":3,"parameter_robustness":2,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":3},"scope":"Generation 7 effect-matched controls","statement":"An unconditional scalar pair control can be matched to aggregate passage in a way that still leaves the state-resolved higher-order pattern unmatched. Aggregate agreement is not state-resolved agreement.","status":"qualified","structural_roles":["projection_loss","negative_finding"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"6aa898aafbdd6bdd1cde715cc36022a16a5acaf1","created_generation":"007B","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-007b-two-level-pair-face-control.md"],"finding_id":"F007-SELECTIVITY-SURVIVES","literal_value":{"primary_expressions":20,"robustness_targets":10},"magnitude_class":"moderate","notes":"","observable":"triad selectivity of the passage after aggregate matching","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":4,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":4,"replication":4},"scope":"Generation 7B two-level pair-face control, 30 target singletons","statement":"After a two-level pair-face control has matched the two aggregate passage numbers, the control remains triad-flat and the higher-order target does not. Hidden-state selectivity survives lower-order scalar matching.","status":"active","structural_roles":["gate","projection_loss"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"d8c97964850194577ecf084a0fb00c209378957c","created_generation":"005","epistemic_layer":"INFERENCE","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-005-targeted-tp-pp-pairs.md"],"finding_id":"F008-COMPOSITION-REPRESENTATION","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"Inference from the spread of residuals, including rows where adding a pairwise rule decreases the triad spread.","observable":"interaction residual across motifs and directions","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":3,"exactness":3,"parameter_robustness":2,"projection_robustness":2,"replication":3},"scope":"Generation 5 interaction census","statement":"The magnitude of a two-rule interaction residual depends on the representation and the source graph. It is not, by itself, a stable discriminator of higher-order structure.","status":"active","structural_roles":["interaction"],"temporal_character":"unknown"}
{"created_commit":"6aa898aafbdd6bdd1cde715cc36022a16a5acaf1","created_generation":"007B","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-007b-two-level-pair-face-control.md"],"finding_id":"F009-TWO-LEVEL-COLLAPSE","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"moderate","notes":"The report's wording is that the lower-order representation uses the two slots as one unconditional weight.","observable":"fitted pair-face weights against the higher-order target","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":4,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":4,"replication":3},"scope":"Generation 7B","statement":"The two-parameter pair-face representation that matches aggregate passage uses its two slots as one unconditional weight. It does not carry the higher-order selectivity.","status":"active","structural_roles":["equivalence","projection_loss"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"a9d35503f86521b4e8046a03b9a6250143594dc3","created_generation":"008","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008-exploration-synthesis.md"],"finding_id":"F010-OCCUPANCY-AXIS","literal_value":{"S01":0.0645,"S05":-0.0617,"S09":0.2399,"S10":0.1684,"S12":-0.0841,"S16":-0.1396,"three_edge_layer":0.314},"magnitude_class":"large","notes":"Large on this coordinate. Not, by itself, specific to a higher-order reading: unconditional pair rules move it further.","observable":"dense-minus-sparse class occupancy","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":3,"parameter_robustness":4,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":4},"scope":"Generation 8 Rounds 0\u20132, N=4, O=3, H=0, horizon 512","statement":"Mode B exploration finds a large finite-grade sparse/dense occupancy axis. On the S01 expression the four grades are ordered +0.0645, +0.0389, -0.0429, -0.0841 in dense minus sparse. Suppress moves pair epochs toward 4\u20136 edges. Favour moves them toward 0\u20132. Unconditional grades move the axis further than conditional grades.","status":"active","structural_roles":["occupancy_shift","bias"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"6a8060b0a336a9a140eee9816c0db68cf72fefd2","created_generation":"008A","epistemic_layer":"METHODOLOGICAL","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008a-context-repair-synthesis.md"],"finding_id":"F011-QUOTIENT-INVALID","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"","observable":"orbit quotient versus the 16 raw triads","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":4,"replication":4},"scope":"Generation 8A context repair","statement":"Graph-only hidden-context quotienting is formally invalid for labelled rules. The wrong symmetry was real. On this palette it did not hide a large first-destination effect.","status":"active","structural_roles":["methodological_correction"],"temporal_character":"not_applicable"}
{"created_commit":"6a8060b0a336a9a140eee9816c0db68cf72fefd2","created_generation":"008A","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008a-context-repair-synthesis.md"],"finding_id":"F012-RAW-CONTEXT-AXIS","literal_value":{"R01":0.0723,"R03":0.1728,"R05":0.2378,"R05_three_edge":0.3072,"R06":-0.0854,"R07":-0.1448},"magnitude_class":"large","notes":"","observable":"dense-minus-sparse occupancy under exhaustive context","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":3,"parameter_robustness":4,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":5},"scope":"Generation 8A, 6144 episodes, 16 raw triads, horizon 512","statement":"Exhaustive raw-context starts preserve the edge-count axis. Copied dense-minus-sparse values include R03 +0.1728, R01 +0.0723, R04 +0.0691, R00 +0.0033, R02 -0.0711, R06 -0.0854, R07 -0.1448, and composite R05 +0.2378. The 3-edge layer stays near 0.314.","status":"active","structural_roles":["occupancy_shift"],"temporal_character":"finite_horizon_integrated"}
{"created_commit":"6a8060b0a336a9a140eee9816c0db68cf72fefd2","created_generation":"008A","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008a-context-repair-synthesis.md"],"finding_id":"F008A-PLUGIN-INITIAL-MI","literal_value":{"checkpoint_plugin_nats":0.12,"first_destination_max_nats":0.0702,"unit":"nats"},"magnitude_class":"small","notes":"The measured plug-in values stand. Their reading as persistent triad information does not.","observable":"plug-in mutual information","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":2,"exactness":2,"parameter_robustness":2,"projection_robustness":2,"replication":3},"scope":"Generation 8A finite contingency tables, 16 replicates","statement":"Under the uniform raw prior, the plug-in mutual information about the first other 3-edge destination is 0.0127 to 0.0702 nats. The largest cell is 0.0702 nats. Checkpoint plug-in class information stays near 0.12 nats through pair epoch 512.","status":"historical_observation","structural_roles":["memory"],"temporal_character":"unknown"}
{"created_commit":"72f77430352ab6fa76dfe314992ed4494c1e1a1c","created_generation":"008B","epistemic_layer":"METHODOLOGICAL","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008b-information-calibration.md"],"finding_id":"F013-PLUGIN-OVERSTATES","literal_value":{"R03_star_plugin_nats":0.07021,"cells":336,"null_mean_nats":[0.03024,0.03127],"reproduction_gap":2.81e-16},"magnitude_class":"small","notes":"Commit 7eb63924c4c5484decd1ab5b7bee3a25b440ac68 corrected a validation assertion. The structural zero remains the full labelled pair mask, not the isomorphism class.","observable":"plug-in minus permutation null, compared with the exact kernel","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":4,"replication":4},"scope":"Generation 8B calibration of the Generation 8A tables","statement":"Plug-in mutual information from these finite tables substantially overstates hidden-context information. 336 Generation 8A cells reproduce with maximum absolute gap 2.810e-16. First-destination permutation-null means are 0.03024 to 0.03127 nats. The largest plug-in cell, R03 star at 0.07021 nats, is a structural-zero system whose exact value is below 1e-10.","status":"active","structural_roles":["methodological_correction"],"temporal_character":"not_applicable"}
{"created_commit":"dc9f9b9eb6e4a36b4513d10b49e937c43b57b371","created_generation":"008B","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008b-information-calibration.md"],"finding_id":"F014-EXACT-FIRST-DESTINATION","literal_value":{"floor_nats":1e-10,"maximum_nats":2.025e-05,"unit":"nats"},"magnitude_class":"very_small","notes":"functional_significance is unknown.","observable":"I(initial raw triad; first other 3-edge class)","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":2,"projection_robustness":4,"replication":4},"scope":"A0 palette, exact pair-event epoch kernel, uniform raw triad","statement":"Exact first-destination mutual information is at the 1e-10 floor for R00, R03, and R07, and for every path source. On star and triangle the conditioned values are R01 5.699e-7, R02 3.307e-7, R04 3.307e-7, R05 2.025e-5, and R06 1.906e-7 nats. Star and triangle agree to about 1e-16.","status":"active","structural_roles":["routing","negative_finding"],"temporal_character":"transient"}
{"created_commit":"dc9f9b9eb6e4a36b4513d10b49e937c43b57b371","created_generation":"008B","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008b-information-calibration.md"],"finding_id":"F015-TRANSIENT-CLASS-MEMORY","literal_value":{"checkpoint_32_nats":1.29e-09,"floor_epoch":64,"max_checkpoint_1_nats":0.02798},"magnitude_class":"small","notes":"","observable":"I(initial triad; graph class at pair epoch k)","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":2,"projection_robustness":4,"replication":4},"scope":"A0 palette, pair-event checkpoints through 512","statement":"Exact initial-context graph-class information is transient. The largest value is R06 path at checkpoint 1, 0.02798 nats. By checkpoint 32 the largest exact class value is about 1.29e-9 nats. By checkpoint 64 every exact class value is below 1e-10. The labelled pair mask decays on the same schedule. The plug-in figure near 0.12 to 0.14 nats through epoch 512 is not persistent information.","status":"active","structural_roles":["forgetting","memory"],"temporal_character":"transient"}
{"created_commit":"dc9f9b9eb6e4a36b4513d10b49e937c43b57b371","created_generation":"008B","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008b-information-calibration.md"],"finding_id":"F016-CURRENT-SLOT-INFORMATION","literal_value":{"R01_R02_R04_balanced_nats":0.009749,"R05_balanced_nats":0.010413,"R06_balanced_nats":0.023368,"unit":"nats"},"magnitude_class":"small","notes":"Small on the nat scale. Exact under the kernel. The structural role is a gate, not a long memory.","observable":"I(current triad; next pair slot | full labelled pair mask)","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":4,"replication":4},"scope":"A0 palette, six pair propensities renormalised on the next event being a pair event","statement":"The current triad carries exact local next-slot information only where the rule reads triadic state. Balanced full-mask CMI is at the floor for R00, R03, and R07. It is 0.009749 nats for R01, R02, and R04, 0.010413 for R05, and 0.023368 for R06. Stationary pair-event values are 0.012025, 0.013240, and 0.016895 on those same groups.","status":"active","structural_roles":["gate","bias"],"temporal_character":"local"}
{"created_commit":"dc9f9b9eb6e4a36b4513d10b49e937c43b57b371","created_generation":"008B","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008b-information-calibration.md"],"finding_id":"F017-CLASS-PROJECTION-LOSS","literal_value":{"R01_retained_fraction":0.661,"R06_retained_fraction":0.443,"next_class_nats":[0.001,0.0026]},"magnitude_class":"moderate","notes":"","observable":"I(current triad; next pair slot | graph class) / I(current triad; next pair slot | full mask)","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":2,"projection_robustness":5,"replication":4},"scope":"stationary pair-event weighting","statement":"Replacing the full labelled pair mask by graph isomorphism class retains 0.661 of the stationary next-slot CMI for R01, R02, and R04, 0.710 for R05, and 0.443 for R06. The discarded fraction is labelled alignment. Information in the next graph class given the current graph class is about 0.001 to 0.0026 nats.","status":"active","structural_roles":["projection_loss"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"72f77430352ab6fa76dfe314992ed4494c1e1a1c","created_generation":"008B","epistemic_layer":"INFERENCE","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008b-information-calibration.md"],"finding_id":"F018-LOCAL-VERSUS-INITIAL","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"Inference from F015 and F016. It is not a claim that the grammar ought to remember.","observable":"comparison of I(T0; Pk) with I(Tk; next slot | Pk)","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":2,"projection_robustness":4,"replication":4},"scope":"H=0 grammar of Generations 8\u20138B","statement":"Local higher-order dependence and long-lived initial-condition memory are distinct. The current triad can alter the next pair slot after the initial triad has been forgotten by the visible pair process.","status":"active","structural_roles":["gate","forgetting"],"temporal_character":"local"}
{"created_commit":"dc9f9b9eb6e4a36b4513d10b49e937c43b57b371","created_generation":"008B","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008b-information-calibration.md"],"finding_id":"F008-EDGE-VERSUS-SHAPE","literal_value":{"R01_path_shape_nats":0.008838,"R06_path_shape_nats":0.01918},"magnitude_class":"small","notes":"This is a primary input to the Generation 8C mechanism reading. The mechanism itself is not asserted here.","observable":"I(T0; class), I(T0; edge count), I(T0; class | edge count)","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":2,"projection_robustness":5,"replication":4},"scope":"checkpoint 1 of the pair-event clock","statement":"At checkpoint 1, star and triangle carry only edge-count information: class information equals edge-count information and the shape term is 0. Path carries an extra shape term. For R06 path the split is 0.02798 class, 0.008801 edge, 0.01918 shape. For R01 path it is 0.01023, 0.001393, and 0.008838. The edge term agrees between path and star to about 1e-16.","status":"active","structural_roles":["shape_selection","occupancy_shift"],"temporal_character":"transient"}
{"created_commit":"dc9f9b9eb6e4a36b4513d10b49e937c43b57b371","created_generation":"008B","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008b-information-calibration.md"],"finding_id":"F008B-FINITE-HORIZON-RANGE","literal_value":{"R01":0.001423,"R06":0.001925,"grade_scale":0.1},"magnitude_class":"very_small","notes":"","observable":"max minus min dense-minus-sparse across 16 raw triads","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":2,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":4},"scope":"mean class occupancy over pair epochs 1 through 512","statement":"Exact dense-minus-sparse context ranges over 512 pair epochs are at the floor for R00, R03, and R07. Conditioned ranges are R01 0.001423, R02 0.000395, R04 0.000395, R05 0.000347, and R06 0.001925. They are genuine finite-horizon integrals and small beside grade-driven occupancy shifts of order 10^-1. The Generation 8A raw-context spans near 0.06 to 0.09 were mostly sampling variation.","status":"active","structural_roles":["occupancy_shift","memory"],"temporal_character":"finite_horizon_integrated"}
{"created_commit":"72f77430352ab6fa76dfe314992ed4494c1e1a1c","created_generation":"008B","epistemic_layer":"OPEN_QUESTION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008b-information-calibration.md"],"finding_id":"Q-PATH-SHAPE","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"Raised by F008-EDGE-VERSUS-SHAPE. A robustness vector of zeros marks an open question, not a weak finding. Status set to qualified in Generation 8C. The statement is unchanged.","observable":"I(T0; class | edge count)","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":0,"exactness":0,"parameter_robustness":0,"projection_robustness":0,"replication":0},"scope":"checkpoint 1, canonical 3-edge sources","statement":"Why does path topology convert early triadic context into shape information at the first pair event, while star and triangle convert it only into edge count?","status":"qualified","structural_roles":["open_question","shape_selection"],"temporal_character":"transient"}
{"created_commit":"72f77430352ab6fa76dfe314992ed4494c1e1a1c","created_generation":"008B","epistemic_layer":"OPEN_QUESTION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008b-information-calibration.md"],"finding_id":"Q-LOCAL-SLOT","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"Status set to qualified in Generation 8C. The statement is unchanged.","observable":"balanced I(current triad; next pair slot | full mask)","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":0,"exactness":0,"parameter_robustness":0,"projection_robustness":0,"replication":0},"scope":"single conditional pair rules on the A0 palette","statement":"What minimal state coordinates and normalisation produce the balanced full-mask slot informations 0.009749 and 0.023368 nats?","status":"qualified","structural_roles":["open_question","gate"],"temporal_character":"local"}
{"created_commit":"72f77430352ab6fa76dfe314992ed4494c1e1a1c","created_generation":"008B","epistemic_layer":"OPEN_QUESTION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008b-information-calibration.md"],"finding_id":"Q-CLASS-REMAINDER","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"Status set to qualified in Generation 8C. The statement is unchanged.","observable":"full-mask CMI minus class-conditioned CMI","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":0,"exactness":0,"parameter_robustness":0,"projection_robustness":0,"replication":0},"scope":"stationary pair-event weighting","statement":"Which labelled alignments inside a graph class carry the slot information that isomorphism projection discards, and why does R06 lose a larger fraction than R01?","status":"qualified","structural_roles":["open_question","projection_loss"],"temporal_character":"stationary"}
{"created_commit":"72f77430352ab6fa76dfe314992ed4494c1e1a1c","created_generation":"008B","epistemic_layer":"OPEN_QUESTION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008b-information-calibration.md"],"finding_id":"Q-H-POSITIVE","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"","observable":"persistence of a higher-order influence when history is a constraint coordinate","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":0,"exactness":0,"parameter_robustness":0,"projection_robustness":0,"replication":0},"scope":"future fork, H>0, not executed in Generation 8C","statement":"What changes when relational history itself becomes part of the constraint state? Rapid forgetting in the present H=0 grammar is an observation about that grammar, not a defect to be repaired inside it.","status":"qualified","structural_roles":["open_question","memory"],"temporal_character":"unknown"}
{"created_commit":"a9d35503f86521b4e8046a03b9a6250143594dc3","created_generation":"008","epistemic_layer":"OPEN_QUESTION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008-exploration-synthesis.md"],"finding_id":"Q-SCALE-N","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"","observable":"local slot law and edge-count occupancy at larger N","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":0,"exactness":0,"parameter_robustness":0,"projection_robustness":0,"replication":0},"scope":"not executed; N=4 is the present grammar","statement":"How does the local gate, the normalisation, and the occupancy axis scale when N moves past 4 while the same local-rule grammar is kept?","status":"unresolved","structural_roles":["open_question"],"temporal_character":"unknown"}
{"created_commit":"a9d35503f86521b4e8046a03b9a6250143594dc3","created_generation":"008","epistemic_layer":"OPEN_QUESTION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008-exploration-synthesis.md","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008a-context-repair-synthesis.md"],"finding_id":"Q-THREE-EDGE-LAYER","literal_value":{"near":0.314},"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"","observable":"share of 3-edge isomorphism classes","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":0,"exactness":0,"parameter_robustness":0,"projection_robustness":0,"replication":0},"scope":"Generation 8 and 8A finite-horizon occupancy","statement":"What keeps the 3-edge occupancy layer near 0.314 across the Generation 8 palette?","status":"unresolved","structural_roles":["open_question","occupancy_shift"],"temporal_character":"finite_horizon_integrated"}
{"created_commit":"72f77430352ab6fa76dfe314992ed4494c1e1a1c","created_generation":"008B","epistemic_layer":"RS_GLOBAL_COHERENCE_INTERPRETATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008b-information-calibration.md"],"finding_id":"F-RS-SEPARATION","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"Interpretation. Not an observation and not a design conclusion.","observable":null,"robustness_vector":{"control_separation":3,"exactness":2,"parameter_robustness":1,"projection_robustness":2,"replication":2},"scope":"interpretation of the H=0 laboratory grammar only","statement":"A small exact local dependence of a lower-order event on a current higher-order bit, together with rapid forgetting of that bit's initial value, is compatible with a grammar in which higher-order state modulates present transitions without storing a long initial-condition memory. This does not establish that a physical or biological system uses this mechanism.","status":"active","structural_roles":["gate","forgetting"],"temporal_character":"not_applicable"}
