{"created_commit":"f962000d7c6c750565843426d46bcd3fdbb43026","created_generation":"008C","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008c-round-c0-tables.json","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008c-mechanistic-decomposition.md"],"finding_id":"F8C-CLOSED-FORM-CMI","literal_value":{"favour":0.02336844477204944,"suppress":0.009748566529643857,"unit":"nats"},"magnitude_class":"small","notes":"The state-count factor 1/2 is an enumeration, not a fit. functional_significance is unknown.","observable":"I(current triad; next pair slot | full pair mask)","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":5,"replication":5},"scope":"balanced weighting of R01, R02, R04, and R06","statement":"An inactive single pair rule gives probability 1/6 on each of the six slots. An active rule with one slot multiplied by m gives that slot probability m/(m+5) and each other slot probability 1/(m+5). Half the pair masks are admissible and, on those masks, half the triads match the one-bit gate, so the balanced conditional mutual information is one half of the equal-weight Jensen-Shannon divergence of the two laws. At m=1/4 the value is 0.009748566529643857 nats. At m=4 it is 0.023368444772049440 nats. The enumeration gap is at most 1.114e-15.","status":"active","structural_roles":["gate","normalisation_effect","bias"],"temporal_character":"local"}
{"created_commit":"f962000d7c6c750565843426d46bcd3fdbb43026","created_generation":"008C","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008c-round-c0-tables.json","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008c-mechanistic-decomposition.md"],"finding_id":"F8C-GRADE-ASYMMETRY","literal_value":{"favour_total_variation":0.2777777777777778,"ratio":"7/3","suppress_total_variation":0.11904761904761904},"magnitude_class":"small","notes":"The informations themselves remain small on the nat scale. The asymmetry is a normalisation identity.","observable":"total variation and balanced CMI of q_m against the uniform slot law","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":3,"projection_robustness":5,"replication":5},"scope":"one active pair slot, six-slot normalisation, W4 strong grades","statement":"At m=1/4 the action slot has probability 1/21 and each other slot has probability 4/21. Total variation from the uniform six-slot law is 5/42. At m=4 the action slot has probability 4/9 and each other slot has probability 1/9. Total variation is 5/18. The ratio of those total variations is 7/3, which is also the ratio of the balanced informations' Jensen-Shannon terms and of the closed-form edge drifts. Five unweighted slots remain in the normalising total, so the reciprocal grades sit at different distances from uniformity.","status":"qualified","structural_roles":["normalisation_effect","bias"],"temporal_character":"local"}
