{"created_commit":"093e460e9992e3ddc4fd24cdb43d6d5397de4e29","created_generation":"008D","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008d-round-d0-tables.json","constraint-lab/reports/tables/generation-008d-identities.json","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008d-two-gate-composition-atlas.md"],"finding_id":"F8D-LOG-ADDITIVITY","literal_value":{"kernel_gap":0,"max_log_residual":2.220446049250313e-16,"systems":3584},"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"Feature composition only. It does not say that probabilities, informations, drifts, or trajectory observables add.","observable":"log w(x,e) - (lambda1 phi1(x,e) + lambda2 phi2(x,e))","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":4,"projection_robustness":1,"replication":5},"scope":"Generation 8D Round D0, all 3584 W4 weighted two-rule T->P systems at N=4, H=0, balanced weighting where information is named","statement":"On every one of the 3584 weighted two-rule systems, the implementation kernel weights equal the product of the two rules' multipliers on all 1024 states as exact fractions. The combined log weight minus the sum of the two rules' log-weight features is at most 2.22e-16 on every state and pair slot. Each feature is the conjunction of the action's admissibility literal and one gate literal.","status":"active","structural_roles":["interaction","expressiveness"],"temporal_character":"local"}
{"created_commit":"093e460e9992e3ddc4fd24cdb43d6d5397de4e29","created_generation":"008D","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008d-round-d0-tables.json","constraint-lab/reports/tables/generation-008d-identities.json","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008d-two-gate-composition-atlas.md"],"finding_id":"F8D-NORMALISATION-INTERACTION","literal_value":{"different_action_systems":2480,"gap":"0/1","same_action_systems":272},"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"The coupling of slot probabilities is through the shared denominator. It is called normalisation interaction, not a new interaction term in the rule algebra.","observable":"both-active six-slot law against the closed forms","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":4,"projection_robustness":1,"replication":5},"scope":"Generation 8D Round D0, all 3584 W4 weighted two-rule T->P systems at N=4, H=0, balanced weighting where information is named","statement":"When two rules on different slots are both active the pair law is m1/(m1+m2+4), m2/(m1+m2+4), and 1/(m1+m2+4) on the other four slots. When two rules on one slot are both active it is m1*m2/(m1*m2+5) and 1/(m1*m2+5). Both forms hold with exact-fraction gap 0 on every realised both-active state of 2480 different-action and 272 same-action systems. Opposite literals of one gate and opposite directions on one slot never activate both rules.","status":"active","structural_roles":["normalisation_effect","interaction"],"temporal_character":"local"}
{"created_commit":"093e460e9992e3ddc4fd24cdb43d6d5397de4e29","created_generation":"008D","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008d-round-d0-tables.json","constraint-lab/reports/tables/generation-008d-weighted-systems.json","constraint-lab/reports/tables/generation-008d-identities.json","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008d-two-gate-composition-atlas.md"],"finding_id":"F8D-COMPLEMENTARY-ELIMINATION","literal_value":{"R1T_systems":48,"R1U_systems":16,"kernel_gap":0},"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"Equality of the full weight table is equality of the full-event kernel, so the elimination holds for every global quantity of these systems.","observable":"full-event weight table against the unconditional comparator","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":5,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":5},"scope":"Generation 8D Round D0, all 3584 W4 weighted two-rule T->P systems at N=4, H=0, balanced weighting where information is named","statement":"A | G => m together with A | NOT G => m has the same full ten-slot weight table as the unconditional rule A => m on all 1024 states. All 16 equal-weight complementary systems are of this kind, and the face and non-face placements of the eliminated gate give the same labelled law. With unequal weights the gate partitions the action into two levels: all 48 such systems are a two-level gate law with three rows, which the DSL cannot write as one primitive rule.","status":"active","structural_roles":["equivalence","symmetry","negative_finding"],"temporal_character":"local"}
{"created_commit":"093e460e9992e3ddc4fd24cdb43d6d5397de4e29","created_generation":"008D","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/tables/generation-008d-weighted-systems.json","constraint-lab/reports/tables/generation-008d-truth-tables.jsonl","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008d-two-gate-composition-atlas.md"],"finding_id":"F8D-DIRECTION-ELIMINATION","literal_value":{"example":"ORB-0026-W00","minimal_coordinate_count":1,"systems":16},"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"The direction analogue of complementary-gate elimination. Admissibility is a literal on the slot's bit, and equal weights on its two values remove it.","observable":"minimal raw coordinates of the six-slot law","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":5,"projection_robustness":2,"replication":5},"scope":"Generation 8D Round D0, all 3584 W4 weighted two-rule T->P systems at N=4, H=0, balanced weighting where information is named","statement":"A formation and a dissolution of one slot, on the same triad literal with equal weights, give a law that reads only the gate. The slot's own bit is not a coordinate. All 16 such systems have one minimal coordinate and two rows: the slot carries m whenever the literal is true, in either edge state.","status":"active","structural_roles":["equivalence","symmetry","gate"],"temporal_character":"local"}
{"created_commit":"093e460e9992e3ddc4fd24cdb43d6d5397de4e29","created_generation":"008D","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008d-round-d0-tables.json","constraint-lab/reports/tables/generation-008d-identities.json","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008d-two-gate-composition-atlas.md"],"finding_id":"F8D-NO-GATE-PRODUCT","literal_value":{"delta12":0,"systems":272,"xor_two_gates":false},"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"The XOR statement is exact algebra on the affine form. The measured identity is Delta12 L = 0. The bound concerns two gate literals, not a slot bit and a gate bit.","observable":"logit interaction Delta12 L on the same action","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":5,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":5,"projection_robustness":2,"replication":5},"scope":"Generation 8D Round D0, all 3584 W4 weighted two-rule T->P systems at N=4, H=0, balanced weighting where information is named","statement":"On one action slot with two distinct gates, L11 - L10 - L01 + L00 = 0 on all 272 systems. The log multiplier is c + lambda1 l1(G1) + lambda2 l2(G2). The both-active level is fixed by the other three, no independent conjunction coefficient exists, and an XOR of two gate literals is not representable by two primitive one-gate rules under any choice of literals or weights. The nearest shape, L11 = L00, requires L10 = -L01.","status":"qualified","structural_roles":["expressiveness","negative_finding"],"temporal_character":"local"}
{"created_commit":"093e460e9992e3ddc4fd24cdb43d6d5397de4e29","created_generation":"008D","epistemic_layer":"OBSERVATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/tables/generation-008d-weighted-systems.json","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008d-two-gate-composition-atlas.md"],"finding_id":"F8D-RECIPROCAL-TWINS","literal_value":{"cross_orbit_labelled":24,"cross_orbit_s4":32,"example":["ORB-0003-W01","ORB-0056-W04"],"local_law_classes":3552,"systems":3584},"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"Systems in one local-law class have S4-conjugate full-event kernels.","observable":"labelled and S4 law hashes across structural orbits","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":4,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":4,"projection_robustness":4,"replication":5},"scope":"Generation 8D Round D0, all 3584 W4 weighted two-rule T->P systems at N=4, H=0, balanced weighting where information is named","statement":"On one slot the local law determines the affine log multiplier c + beta1 G1 + beta2 G2, not the literals that wrote it. Flipping both literals and inverting both weights leaves the law unchanged exactly when m1*m2 = 1. Sixteen labelled-law coincidences across orbits, and eight more under vertex permutation, are of this kind. With the eight complementary eliminations they are all of the cross-orbit coincidences: 24 labelled and 32 under S4.","status":"active","structural_roles":["equivalence","symmetry"],"temporal_character":"local"}
