{"created_commit":"093e460e9992e3ddc4fd24cdb43d6d5397de4e29","created_generation":"008D","epistemic_layer":"INFERENCE","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008d-two-gate-composition-atlas.md"],"finding_id":"F8D-ADDITIVE-FEATURE-GRAMMAR","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"Stated only for this DSL. Probability, occupancy, and trajectory observables need not compose additively.","observable":"local composition grammar","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":3,"exactness":4,"parameter_robustness":4,"projection_robustness":2,"replication":4},"scope":"two primitive one-gate T->P rules at N=4, H=0, W4 and general positive multipliers","statement":"In the current multiplicative-weight DSL, constraints compose as additive features in event-logit space, and a system's local law is the softmax of its active features. What cardinality two adds over one gate is two-bit dependence through additive levels, multi-slot bias with a shared denominator, gate partitions, switched gate reading, and slot-gate XOR. It cannot add a gate-by-gate coefficient.","status":"qualified","structural_roles":["expressiveness","interaction","normalisation_effect"],"temporal_character":"local"}
{"created_commit":"093e460e9992e3ddc4fd24cdb43d6d5397de4e29","created_generation":"008D","epistemic_layer":"INFERENCE","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008d-two-gate-composition-atlas.md"],"finding_id":"F8D-SYNTAX-CAN-VANISH","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"Not generalised beyond the demonstrated grammar.","observable":"relation between rule syntax and local law","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":3,"exactness":5,"parameter_robustness":4,"projection_robustness":3,"replication":4},"scope":"two-rule T->P systems of Generation 8D Round D0","statement":"Contextual syntax can be dynamically redundant. Complementary conditions with one weight remove the condition. Opposite directions on one literal with one weight remove the slot state. Reciprocal weights on flipped literals make two texts one kernel. The local law determines the affine logit, not the rule text.","status":"active","structural_roles":["equivalence","negative_finding"],"temporal_character":"local"}
{"created_commit":"093e460e9992e3ddc4fd24cdb43d6d5397de4e29","created_generation":"008D","epistemic_layer":"RS_GLOBAL_COHERENCE_INTERPRETATION","evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/reports/generation-008d-two-gate-composition-atlas.md"],"finding_id":"F8D-RS-COMPOSITIONAL-BOUND","literal_value":null,"magnitude_class":"not_applicable","notes":"It does not establish that nature uses this DSL. It does not infer a designer.","observable":"interpretation of the D0 grammar","robustness_vector":{"control_separation":1,"exactness":2,"parameter_robustness":2,"projection_robustness":1,"replication":2},"scope":"Generation 8D; not a claim about physical or biological systems","statement":"Inside this model a small constraint grammar is compositional in event-logit space and bounded: two higher-order constraints can express a two-dimensional relational dependence that no single constraint expresses, and cannot express a relation between their two conditions. Visible dynamics come from normalisation, occupancy, and topology. A coherence account built on this grammar should attach meaning to the law, the affine logit and its placement, and not to the rule text.","status":"qualified","structural_roles":["expressiveness"],"temporal_character":"not_applicable"}
