{"theorem_id":"CL-T26","title":"History-conditioned same-state divergent futures","status":"ALGEBRAIC_THEOREM","statement":"Two legal equal-probability event-order histories from one augmented start end at identical complete material x but have different full and pair future rows iff m!=1.","assumptions":["Common controller, m, baseline, support and clock","x0 has only 01, no triads; h0=None","Histories form(23),form(12) and the reverse order"],"scope":"RECENT-REVERSAL(m), m>0, N=4 O=3 independent relations; H_pair=1, G=S=L=0.","proof_or_verification":{"proof_sketch":"Commuting toggles reach pair mask 41 and zero triads. Path probabilities are 1/[10(m+9)]. Remembered slots exchange m/D and 1/D with D=m+9 or m+5.","derivation_ref":"constraint-lab/formal/history.md#cl-t26"},"source_generations":["008H"],"evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/formal/history.md","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008h-history-as-state.md","constraint-lab/tests/test_v08h.py"],"coherence_refs":["Q-H-POSITIVE","F8G-FORMAL-H-L-DISTINCTION","F8H-SAME-STATE-DIVERGENT-FUTURES","F8H-CURRENT-VS-INITIAL-MEMORY","F8H-H-QUESTION-RESOLUTION","Q-H-CONSEQUENTIAL-FUNCTIONS"],"counterexample_scope":"Both rows coincide at m=1; comparing distinct programs or different initial registers is not this witness.","dependencies":[],"notes":"Symbolic predeclared expectation before freeze; post-freeze finite rational and numerical checks are separate CL-F05/CL-N07. Representation-relative model statement."}
{"theorem_id":"CL-T27","title":"Non-lumpability of history erasure","status":"ALGEBRAIC_THEOREM","statement":"The full-event and pair-epoch projections forgetting h are strongly lumpable iff m=1.","assumptions":["Projection (x,h)->x or (pair_mask,h)->pair_mask","Strong lumpability means equality into every projected transition block"],"scope":"RECENT-REVERSAL(m), m>0, N=4 O=3 independent relations; H_pair=1, G=S=L=0.","proof_or_verification":{"proof_sketch":"At x*, the block toggling 12 receives m/D versus 1/D. At m=1 all full/pair rows are uniformly independent of h, including the sentinel.","derivation_ref":"constraint-lab/formal/history.md#cl-t27"},"source_generations":["008H"],"evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/formal/history.md","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008h-history-as-state.md","constraint-lab/tests/test_v08h.py"],"coherence_refs":["F8G-FORMAL-EQUIVALENCE-HIERARCHY","F011-QUOTIENT-INVALID","F8H-NONLUMPABLE-MATERIAL-PROJECTION","F8H-TEMPORAL-TESTS-REQUIRED","Q-H-COARSE-GRAINING"],"counterexample_scope":"Non-lumpability rules out a quotient valid for arbitrary augmented initial laws; a selected prior requires a separate process test.","dependencies":["CL-T26","CL-T20"],"notes":"Symbolic predeclared expectation before freeze; post-freeze finite rational and numerical checks are separate CL-F05/CL-N07. Representation-relative model statement."}
{"theorem_id":"CL-T28","title":"Unchanged-state H0 non-compilability","status":"ALGEBRAIC_THEOREM","statement":"For m!=1 no fixed first-order kernel on unchanged complete ordinary x reproduces every history-conditioned projected future row.","assumptions":["One fixed kernel on the unchanged ordinary state space","All reachable history-conditioned rows must be reproduced"],"scope":"RECENT-REVERSAL(m), m>0, N=4 O=3 independent relations; H_pair=1, G=S=L=0.","proof_or_verification":{"proof_sketch":"K0(x*,.) would need to equal the two unequal CL-T26 rows simultaneously, contradicting row uniqueness.","derivation_ref":"constraint-lab/formal/history.md#cl-t28"},"source_generations":["008H"],"evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/formal/history.md","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008h-history-as-state.md","constraint-lab/tests/test_v08h.py"],"coherence_refs":["F8G-FORMAL-CURRENT-STATE-EXPRESSIVITY","F8G-FORMAL-COMPILATION-TEST","Q-H-POSITIVE","F8H-FIXED-STATE-NONCOMPILABILITY","F8H-RS-HISTORY-INTERPRETATION"],"counterexample_scope":"State augmentation, altered update support and marginal-only matching are outside this impossibility theorem.","dependencies":["CL-T26","CL-T12"],"notes":"Symbolic predeclared expectation before freeze; post-freeze finite rational and numerical checks are separate CL-F05/CL-N07. Representation-relative model statement."}
{"theorem_id":"CL-T29","title":"State augmentation restores Markov form","status":"ALGEBRAIC_THEOREM","statement":"RECENT-REVERSAL is first-order Markov on the finite augmented state (x,h).","assumptions":["The register is explicit augmented state","Pair updates set h to the slot; triad updates preserve h"],"scope":"RECENT-REVERSAL(m), m>0, N=4 O=3 independent relations; H_pair=1, G=S=L=0.","proof_or_verification":{"proof_sketch":"The next event row and deterministic augmented update depend only on current (x,h).","derivation_ref":"constraint-lab/formal/history.md#cl-t29"},"source_generations":["008H"],"evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/formal/history.md","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008h-history-as-state.md","constraint-lab/tests/test_v08h.py"],"coherence_refs":["F8G-FORMAL-H-L-DISTINCTION","F8G-FORMAL-COMPILATION-TEST","F8H-AUGMENTED-MARKOV-RESTORATION","F8H-RS-HISTORY-INTERPRETATION"],"counterexample_scope":"An S encoding or binary multibit update is a representation change; no absolute non-Markovianity or irreducible time is established.","dependencies":[],"notes":"Symbolic predeclared expectation before freeze; post-freeze finite rational and numerical checks are separate CL-F05/CL-N07. Representation-relative model statement."}
{"theorem_id":"CL-T30","title":"Exact pair-event quotient closure","status":"ALGEBRAIC_THEOREM","statement":"Summing triad-only excursions gives the exact next-pair kernel on (pair_mask,h), with 384 recurrent states and q_h(e)=m/(m+5) for e=h, otherwise 1/(m+5).","assumptions":["Triad toggles preserve pair mask and h","Unit triad weights; pair weights do not read triad state","The initial sentinel gives uniform pair slots"],"scope":"RECENT-REVERSAL(m), m>0, N=4 O=3 independent relations; H_pair=1, G=S=L=0.","proof_or_verification":{"proof_sketch":"The geometric excursion sum [w_e/(m+9)]/[1-4/(m+9)] equals w_e/(m+5); pair absorption occurs almost surely.","derivation_ref":"constraint-lab/formal/history.md#cl-t30"},"source_generations":["008H"],"evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/formal/history.md","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008h-history-as-state.md","constraint-lab/tests/test_v08h.py"],"coherence_refs":["F011-QUOTIENT-INVALID","F8G-FORMAL-EQUIVALENCE-HIERARCHY","F8H-PAIR-EPOCH-CLOSURE"],"counterexample_scope":"Different history updates or triad-dependent hazards need a new closure proof; no raw-triad prior is assumed.","dependencies":["CL-T29"],"notes":"Symbolic predeclared expectation before freeze; post-freeze finite rational and numerical checks are separate CL-F05/CL-N07. Representation-relative model statement."}
{"theorem_id":"CL-T31","title":"Uniform stationary pair/history law and one-step material equality","status":"ALGEBRAIC_THEOREM","statement":"The recurrent pair-epoch chain has unique uniform stationary joint law pi(p,h)=1/384, independent mask/history, H0 material occupancy and H0 stationary one-step projected pair rows.","assumptions":["m>0; pair-epoch clock after the sentinel","Stationary initial law for the projected one-step comparison"],"scope":"RECENT-REVERSAL(m), m>0, N=4 O=3 independent relations; H_pair=1, G=S=L=0.","proof_or_verification":{"proof_sketch":"Each destination has six predecessors with incoming sum one. Positive slot sequences give irreducibility; parity and a two-step return give period two. Uniform joint law implies independent uniform marginals and averaged slot probability 1/6.","derivation_ref":"constraint-lab/formal/history.md#cl-t31"},"source_generations":["008H"],"evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/formal/history.md","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008h-history-as-state.md","constraint-lab/tests/test_v08h.py"],"coherence_refs":["Q-H-POSITIVE","F8G-FORMAL-EQUIVALENCE-HIERARCHY","F8H-STATIONARY-OCCUPANCY-INVARIANCE","F8H-PROCESS-GRAMMAR-WITHOUT-OCCUPANCY","Q-H-PERSISTENT-STRUCTURE"],"counterexample_scope":"Period two prevents pointwise convergence from fixed parity. Full-event pair-versus-triad hazard and multi-time laws need not match H0.","dependencies":["CL-T30"],"notes":"Symbolic predeclared expectation before freeze; post-freeze finite rational and numerical checks are separate CL-F05/CL-N07. Representation-relative model statement."}
{"theorem_id":"CL-T32","title":"History-slot eigenstructure and initial-history decay","status":"ALGEBRAIC_THEOREM","statement":"The six-slot matrix has eigenvalues 1 and lambda=(m-1)/(m+5) of multiplicity five; Q^k=Pi+lambda^k(I-Pi), and TV from a fixed initial slot is (5/6)|lambda|^k.","assumptions":["Pi is the uniform six-slot rank-one matrix","Pair-event clock; finite m>0"],"scope":"RECENT-REVERSAL(m), m>0, N=4 O=3 independent relations; H_pair=1, G=S=L=0.","proof_or_verification":{"proof_sketch":"Q=Pi+lambda(I-Pi) acts diagonally on constant and zero-sum subspaces; |lambda|<1. Its powers yield the exact conditional row and TV.","derivation_ref":"constraint-lab/formal/history.md#cl-t32"},"source_generations":["008H"],"evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/formal/history.md","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008h-history-as-state.md","constraint-lab/tests/test_v08h.py"],"coherence_refs":["F018-LOCAL-VERSUS-INITIAL","F8C-CURRENT-SURVIVES","F8H-CURRENT-VS-INITIAL-MEMORY"],"counterexample_scope":"Decay concerns initial-slot information in current h, not all initial-condition information in every material multi-time observable.","dependencies":["CL-T30"],"notes":"Symbolic predeclared expectation before freeze; post-freeze finite rational and numerical checks are separate CL-F05/CL-N07. Representation-relative model statement."}
{"theorem_id":"CL-T33","title":"Exactly order-two projected pair-mask process","status":"ALGEBRAIC_THEOREM","statement":"After an observed pair transition the material pair process has order at most two; at stationary law it has exactly order two for m!=1 and is first-order for m=1.","assumptions":["Pair snapshots observe every pair toggle","Positive stationary law for the order-one failure witness"],"scope":"RECENT-REVERSAL(m), m>0, N=4 O=3 independent relations; H_pair=1, G=S=L=0.","proof_or_verification":{"proof_sketch":"The one-hot XOR of previous/current masks identifies h. All earlier snapshots are conditionally irrelevant, while distinct incoming slots into the same current mask give unequal next rows for non-neutral m.","derivation_ref":"constraint-lab/formal/history.md#cl-t33"},"source_generations":["008H"],"evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/formal/history.md","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008h-history-as-state.md","constraint-lab/tests/test_v08h.py"],"coherence_refs":["Q-H-POSITIVE","F8G-FORMAL-EQUIVALENCE-HIERARCHY","F8H-ORDER2-PROJECTED-PROCESS","F8H-TEMPORAL-TESTS-REQUIRED","Q-H-DEPTH"],"counterexample_scope":"No finite Markov-order claim is made for full-event snapshots containing arbitrarily long triad-only waits.","dependencies":["CL-T26","CL-T30","CL-T31"],"notes":"Symbolic predeclared expectation before freeze; post-freeze finite rational and numerical checks are separate CL-F05/CL-N07. Representation-relative model statement."}
{"theorem_id":"CL-T34","title":"Temporal backtracking and consecutive-slot information","status":"ALGEBRAIC_THEOREM","statement":"Stationary pair-mask backtracking is m/(m+5), and consecutive-event MI is ln 6+a ln a+5b ln b, with a=m/(m+5), b=1/(m+5); MI vanishes iff m=1.","assumptions":["Stationary uniform history on the pair clock","Exactly one pair bit toggles at each pair epoch"],"scope":"RECENT-REVERSAL(m), m>0, N=4 O=3 independent relations; H_pair=1, G=S=L=0.","proof_or_verification":{"proof_sketch":"Two toggles restore a mask iff slots repeat. The joint slot law Q_ij/6 has uniform marginals; direct KL gives the expression and strict positivity away from neutral.","derivation_ref":"constraint-lab/formal/history.md#cl-t34"},"source_generations":["008H"],"evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/formal/history.md","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008h-history-as-state.md","constraint-lab/tests/test_v08h.py"],"coherence_refs":["Q-H-POSITIVE","F018-LOCAL-VERSUS-INITIAL","F8H-TEMPORAL-CORRELATION","F8H-CURRENT-VS-INITIAL-MEMORY","F8H-PROCESS-GRAMMAR-WITHOUT-OCCUPANCY","F8H-TEMPORAL-TESTS-REQUIRED"],"counterexample_scope":"A temporal process statistic is distinct from a one-time occupancy or a master memory score.","dependencies":["CL-T31","CL-T32"],"notes":"Symbolic predeclared expectation before freeze; post-freeze finite rational and numerical checks are separate CL-F05/CL-N07. Representation-relative model statement."}
