{"theorem_id":"CL-T88","title":"Matched Kac set recurrence control","status":"ALGEBRAIC_THEOREM","statement":"For a finite irreducible stationary chain, starting from its stationary conditional law on nonempty D gives E[tau_D^+]=1/pi(D). Equal class occupancy therefore forces equal same-class mean positive recurrence, not cross-class MFPT.","assumptions":["Finite irreducible Markov chain, positive stationary conditioning sets","Declared matched source and comparator where asserted","Single-toggle pair-event support where parity/short-return controls are used"],"scope":"Generic finite-chain argument under stated hypotheses; N4 role applications as scoped. No unrestricted H1 exclusion.","proof_or_verification":{"derivation_ref":"constraint-lab/formal/history-controlled-passage.md#kac-control","proof_sketch":"The embedded return chain is stationary under pi restricted to D; excursion occupation normalisation (or stationary visit frequency) gives mean interval one divided by pi(D). Periodicity does not invalidate the identity."},"source_generations":["008N"],"evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/formal/history-controlled-passage.md","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008n-h2-controlled-passage.md","constraint-lab/reports/tables/generation-008n-validation.json","constraint-lab/reports/tables/generation-008n-summary.json","constraint-lab/tests/test_v08n.py"],"coherence_refs":["F8N-KAC-CONTROL"],"counterexample_scope":"No claim of Markov graph-class return process, physical memory, purpose, task benefit or exclusion of hidden-state recodings.","dependencies":["CL-T86"],"notes":"Symbolic proof is distinct from finite palette verification; no all-m promotion of finite nonzero outcomes."}
{"theorem_id":"CL-T89","title":"Adjacent-matched H1 passage exclusion","status":"ALGEBRAIC_THEOREM","statement":"If H2 and Kpi have unequal passage under the declared matched source law, no fixed first-order kernel on exactly (P,h1) matching the full stationary adjacent H1 law reproduces both that law and the H2 passage functional.","assumptions":["Finite irreducible Markov chain, positive stationary conditioning sets","Declared matched source and comparator where asserted","Single-toggle pair-event support where parity/short-return controls are used"],"scope":"Generic finite-chain argument under stated hypotheses; N4 role applications as scoped. No unrestricted H1 exclusion.","proof_or_verification":{"derivation_ref":"constraint-lab/formal/history-controlled-passage.md#matched-h1-exclusion","proof_sketch":"Positive pi_s and adjacent joint J force B(s,s')=J(s,s')/pi_s(s)=Kpi. The stipulated source is then also fixed; an unequal passage functional contradicts simultaneous matching."},"source_generations":["008N"],"evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/formal/history-controlled-passage.md","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008n-h2-controlled-passage.md","constraint-lab/reports/tables/generation-008n-validation.json","constraint-lab/reports/tables/generation-008n-summary.json","constraint-lab/tests/test_v08n.py"],"coherence_refs":["F8N-H1-MATCHED-PASSAGE-BOUNDARY"],"counterexample_scope":"No claim of Markov graph-class return process, physical memory, purpose, task benefit or exclusion of hidden-state recodings.","dependencies":["CL-T82","CL-T85"],"notes":"Symbolic proof is distinct from finite palette verification; no all-m promotion of finite nonzero outcomes."}
{"theorem_id":"CL-T90","title":"Passage transport under kernel conjugacy","status":"ALGEBRAIC_THEOREM","statement":"A bijective kernel conjugacy transporting the stationary source and stopping sets transports first-return totals, length slices, route pieces, MFPT and competing-target probabilities, with target-order complementation when needed.","assumptions":["Finite irreducible Markov chain, positive stationary conditioning sets","Declared matched source and comparator where asserted","Single-toggle pair-event support where parity/short-return controls are used"],"scope":"Generic finite-chain argument under stated hypotheses; N4 role applications as scoped. No unrestricted H1 exclusion.","proof_or_verification":{"derivation_ref":"constraint-lab/formal/history-controlled-passage.md#passage-transport","proof_sketch":"The bijection preserves each finite stopped path probability and time. Sum disjoint first-hit paths or use uniqueness of Dirichlet solutions. Self-conjugacies fixing P4 and exchanging its alternatives force committor one half."},"source_generations":["008N"],"evidence_refs":["constraint-lab/formal/history-controlled-passage.md","constraint-lab/reports/generation-008n-h2-controlled-passage.md","constraint-lab/reports/tables/generation-008n-validation.json","constraint-lab/reports/tables/generation-008n-summary.json","constraint-lab/tests/test_v08n.py"],"coherence_refs":["F8N-CONJUGATE-PASSAGE","F8N-K3-COMMITTOR"],"counterexample_scope":"No claim of Markov graph-class return process, physical memory, purpose, task benefit or exclusion of hidden-state recodings.","dependencies":["CL-T80","CL-T84"],"notes":"Symbolic proof is distinct from finite palette verification; no all-m promotion of finite nonzero outcomes."}
